  "id": "Compound::DB00138 - Gene::11136",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between L-cystine and Slc7a9, mediated through the L-cystine transmembrane transporter activity. Multiple paths indicate that L-cystine binds to Ctns or Slc3a1, which in turn participates in the transport of sulfur amino acids, a process that is ultimately linked to Slc7a9. This suggests that L-cystine may influence Slc7a9 through a common pathway involving sulfur amino acid transport. The high scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for L-cystine in modulating Slc7a9 activity, potentially through the regulation of sulfur amino acid transport, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
